{
    "version": "1.9.12",
    "changelog": "Four things. (1) SAVE FIX - the important one. A bug could make the editor load an old copy of the map stored on this computer instead of the newest map from GitHub, and the next save would then write that old map over the new one (this is what rewrote whole zones on Oct 24). The editor now records exactly which GitHub copy its saved work is based on. Work based on an older copy is never loaded over the newer map: it is set aside in a 'superseded' folder inside the editor's data folder, the fresh download is used, and you are told. Real unpublished edits made on the current copy are still kept, as before. A save now only ever changes the pieces you actually edited - every other record is written back exactly as it came. (2) Delete review: the After picture is now clickable. When deleting several pieces reveals pieces that were underneath them, click a revealed piece in the After picture to add it to the same deletion (if it is one run of a paired object, its partner is added too). The Before picture lights it, the After picture redraws without it, and you can keep clicking to add more. Cancel still restores everything, including your selection. (3) The Delete key on the keyboard now starts the same delete flow as the Delete button, including the 'Nothing is selected' popup. (4) The bottom pane is now the RESOURCE MAP: it shows the reference map the world was built from, at the same place and zoom as the top view, so you can compare where streets are with where they should be; it follows the road you select. Its labels now say so - 'Resource map - reference' - and the elevation line above it is labelled 'Road elevation'.",
